            <div xml:id="d765">

                <pb facs="0729" n="613" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg613"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 815.51/334.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister of Honduras to
                        the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of Honduras</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 16, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary</hi>: It has come to the knowledge of
                    the Government of Honduras that the Convention signed in this capital on the
                    tenth day of January of the year one thousand nine hundred and eleven by his
                    excellency the Secretary of State, Mr. Philander C. Knox, as Plenipotentiary of
                    the Government of the United States, and Don Juan E. Paredes, as Plenipotentiary
                    of the Government of Honduras, is pending in the Senate of this Republic for its
                    ratification. In this connection I have received instructions from the
                    Department of State of the Government of Honduras to apprize your excellency
                    that the said Convention having been submitted to the National Congress for its
                    ratification, by the Government over which General <pb facs="0730" n="614"
                        xml:id="pg614"/> Don Miguel R. Dávila presided, was disapproved by Decree
                    No. 20, issued on the thirty-first day of the month and year above stated, which
                    I have the honor to transcribe to your excellency: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Decree No. 20. The National Congress, having before it the Convention
                            signed in the city of Washington on the tenth of this month, by Señor
                            Don Juan E. Paredes, as Plenipotentiary of Honduras and Mr. Philander C.
                            Knox as Plenipotentiary of the United States of America, and in the
                            exercise of the powers conferred upon it by Article 90, number 22, of
                            the Political Constitution of the State—Decrees: Sole Article. The
                            Convention under consideration is disapproved. Given in Tegucigalpa, in
                            the Hall of Sessions, the thirty-first day of the month of January, one
                            thousand nine hundred and eleven. Francisco Escobar, President; Leandro
                            Valladares, Secretary; Ramón Fiallos, Secretary.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>I avail [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">F. Dávila.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
